  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Solve these simultaneous equations for $(x,y,z)$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x-2y+z&=1\\\\x-y+z&=0\\\\x-y+2z&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(-2,-1,1)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (1) from (2), then subtract (2) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-1\\\\z&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}x-(-1)+1&=0\\\\x+2&=0\\\\x&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(-2,-1,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 84
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+y-3z&=1\\\\2x+y-4z&=7\\\\2x+y-z&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(4,-9,-2)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (2) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}3z&=-6\\\\z&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (1) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}x-z&=6\\\\x-(-2)&=6\\\\x&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}4+y-3(-2)&=1\\\\y+10&=1\\\\y&=-9\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(4,-9,-2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 108
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z&=5\\\\3x+3y+2z&=8\\\\-x+3y+2z&=4\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(1,1,1)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (3) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}4x&=4\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1) and (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}1+2y+2z&=5\\\\y+z&=2\\qquad(4)\\\\-1+3y+2z&=4\\\\3y+2z&=5\\qquad(5)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract twice (4) from (5), then substitute into (4):\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=1\\\\1+z&=2\\\\z&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(1,1,1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 124
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x-y+z&=1\\\\x+y-2z&=1\\\\x+y+2z&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(1,0,0)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (2) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}4z&=0\\\\z&=0\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (1) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}2y+z&=0\\\\2y&=0\\\\y&=0\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}x-0+0&=1\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(1,0,0)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x+y+z&=-4\\\\2x+y+2z&=-3\\\\3x+y+2z&=-1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(2,-5,-1)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (2) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=2\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract twice (1) from (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=5\\\\y&=-5\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}2-5+z&=-4\\\\z-3&=-4\\\\z&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(2,-5,-1)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y+2z&=1\\\\x+y+2z&=8\\\\x+4y+2z&=11\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x,y,z)=(3,1,2)$.",
          "worked": "Number the equations (1), (2) and (3) in order. Subtract (2) from (3):\n$$\\begin{align*}3y&=3\\\\y&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (1) and (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}-2x+3+2z&=1\\\\-2x+2z&=-2\\qquad(4)\\\\x+1+2z&=8\\\\x+2z&=7\\qquad(5)\\end{align*}$$\nSubtract (4) from (5):\n$$\\begin{align*}3x&=9\\\\x&=3\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into (5):\n$$\\begin{align*}3+2z&=7\\\\2z&=4\\\\z&=2\\end{align*}$$\nThus $(x,y,z)=(3,1,2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 140
      }
    ]
  },
